# Frontend testing

## E2E (Playwright)

- Director smoke: `seedDirectorSession` + `seedDirectorEventDetailsMocks` (extend helpers; do not invent a third auth path).
- Mock every API the tab hits (`complete`, director-access, squads, side-actions, tournaments/:id, relationships, etc.).
- Assert one clear composition: event heading + primary workspace signal.
- Prefer role/text that uniquely matches; avoid strict-mode duplicates when headings repeat.
- Label mocked browser workflows clearly and make route mocks fail closed on unhandled APIs.
- Reserve live-backend full flows for specs with explicit environment prerequisites; do not imply a mocked flow proves persistence.

## Unit (Vitest)

- Tests live under `tests/unit/` (not colocated in `src/` today) - keep that layout unless a deliberate migration happens.
- After EventDetails/tab changes, keep mount tests and mocked children in sync.
- Fix orphan mocks when components are split or renamed.
- Export pure helpers from pages/utils and cover them with focused unit tests.
- Coverage thresholds are allowlisted in `vite.config.ts` - do not "fix" coverage by deleting measured files; add tests or consciously expand the allowlist with real coverage.
- Async UI tests must deliberately resolve requests out of order and verify stale successes and failures are ignored.
- API contract changes require type, unit fixture, and Playwright fixture updates in the same commit.

## Product truth

A green test that asserts a sham placeholder is worse than no test - update assertions when the product ships.
